<title>USA: S. Dakota voters pass tax increase restriction.</title>
<headline>S. Dakota voters pass tax increase restriction.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Dakota voters said yes to an amendment requiring voter approval or a super majority -- two-thirds vote of the legislature -- for any new or increased taxes.</p>
<p>Preliminary results reported by the Secretary of State's office indicated the measure passed with 74 percent of the vote.</p>
<p>Another proposed amendment to empower the state investment council to invest state educational funds also passed with 63 percent of the vote, the office reported.</p>
<p>--Karen Pierog, 312-408-8647</p>
</text>
